    {
      "ordinal": 7,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "1.4",
      "title": "Fastening systems requirements",
      "body": "● Tabards can be tied with the following systems:\n○ Buttons made of fabric, wood, bone, or metal.\n○ Laces, made of leather, rope or fabric.\n○ Any other system based on historical sources.\n○ Any modern fastening system is denied. (Zips, snap buttons, velcro, paracord, nylon rope etc.)\n● Tabards can be open on the side, tied with laces.\n● Tabards can be open on the front, and tied with buttons.",
